&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tekion:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Positively disrupting an industry that has not seen any innovation in over 50 years, Tekion has challenged the paradigm with the first and fastest cloud-native automotive platform that includes the revolutionary Automotive Retail Cloud (ARC) for retailers, Automotive Enterprise Cloud (AEC) for manufacturers and other large automotive enterprises and Automotive Partner Cloud (APC) for technology and industry partners. Tekion connects the entire spectrum of the automotive retail ecosystem through one seamless platform. The transformative platform uses cutting-edge technology, big data, machine learning, and AI to seamlessly bring together OEMs, retailers/dealers and consumers. With its highly configurable integration and greater customer engagement capabilities, Tekion is enabling the best automotive retail experiences ever. Tekion employs close to 3,000 people across North America, Asia and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product&amp;nbsp;Manager&amp;nbsp;II&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;Bengaluru,&amp;nbsp;India&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT TEKION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tekion is positively disrupting an industry that has seen little meaningful innovation in over 50 years. With the first cloud-native Automotive Retail Cloud (ARC) and Automotive Enterprise Cloud (AEC), Tekion connects OEMs, dealers, and consumers through a single unified platform powered by real-time data, machine learning, and AI. Tekion employs close to 3,000 people across North America, Asia, and Europe, and is trusted by 1,700+ dealership rooftops globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLE OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a technically grounded and detail-oriented Product Manager II to own the Retail module and Core application layer within Tekion&#39;s Automotive Enterprise Cloud (AEC) platform. This is a platform-facing product role — you will bridge the gap between OEM program requirements and Tekion&#39;s engineering organisation, ensuring that complex business needs from GM, Honda, and other OEM partners are translated into well-defined, scalable platform capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary ownership spans vehicle configuration and inventory, deal structuring workflows, and the Core platform layer — including login, SSO, user roles, and permissions. You will partner closely with OEM program teams to understand requirements first-hand and work with platform engineering to spec, prioritise, and deliver features that meet OEM certification standards while remaining extensible across the platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Own the AEC Retail Module Roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Define and maintain the product roadmap for vehicle configuration, inventory management, and deal structuring workflows within the AEC platform. Translate OEM program requirements into a prioritised, execution-ready backlog.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Drive Core Platform Product Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Own the Core application layer — including user authentication (login/SSO), role-based access control (RBAC), permissions frameworks, and cross-module platform services. Ensure these foundations are robust, configurable, and OEM-certifiable.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Translate OEM Requirements into Platform Specifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Act as the primary product interface between OEM program teams (GM, Honda, and others) and Tekion&#39;s platform engineering organisation. Convert OEM business and functional requirements into clearly scoped platform features, API contracts, and data models.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Own the Scrum Team Backlog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Write precise user stories, acceptance criteria, and feature specs for your engineering squad. Maintain a groomed, well-prioritised backlog that balances OEM program commitments, platform health, and roadmap investments.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Define Vehicle Configuration &amp;amp; Inventory Data Contracts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Collaborate with engineering and data teams to design configuration schemas, inventory data feeds, and pricing rule structures that support multi-OEM requirements while remaining scalable and maintainable.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Support Deal Structuring Workflow Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Understand and document end-to-end deal structuring flows — from vehicle selection and option pricing through to deal presentation — ensuring feature decisions align with both OEM program rules and dealer operational needs.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Drive Cross-Functional Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Coordinate&amp;nbsp;across&amp;nbsp;OEM&amp;nbsp;program&amp;nbsp;teams,&amp;nbsp;platform&amp;nbsp;engineering,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;internal&amp;nbsp;business&amp;nbsp;stakeholders&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;resolve&amp;nbsp;requirement&amp;nbsp;conflicts,&amp;nbsp;manage&amp;nbsp;dependencies,&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;maintain&amp;nbsp;shared&amp;nbsp;delivery&amp;nbsp;timelines.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Track Feature Adoption &amp;amp; Platform Health Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Define success metrics for new platform capabilities — adoption rates, error rates, configuration accuracy, permission incident rates. Iterate on features based on data and OEM program feedback.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Ensure OEM Compliance &amp;amp; Certification Readiness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Validate that platform capabilities meet OEM-mandated compliance, security, and certification standards. Support quarterly program reviews and OEM sign-off processes.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Drive Adoption &amp;amp; Change Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Partner&amp;nbsp;with&amp;nbsp;program&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;business&amp;nbsp;teams&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;build&amp;nbsp;rollout&amp;nbsp;plans&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;enablement&amp;nbsp;materials&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;new&amp;nbsp;platform&amp;nbsp;features,&amp;nbsp;ensuring&amp;nbsp;smooth&amp;nbsp;adoption&amp;nbsp;across&amp;nbsp;OEM&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;internal&amp;nbsp;user&amp;nbsp;groups.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SKILLS &amp;amp; QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• 3–5 years of Product Management experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In&amp;nbsp;platform,&amp;nbsp;enterprise&amp;nbsp;SaaS,&amp;nbsp;or&amp;nbsp;OEM/B2B&amp;nbsp;technology&amp;nbsp;products.&amp;nbsp;Experience&amp;nbsp;owning&amp;nbsp;both&amp;nbsp;functional&amp;nbsp;features&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;foundational&amp;nbsp;platform&amp;nbsp;capabilities&amp;nbsp;(auth,&amp;nbsp;permissions,&amp;nbsp;configuration)&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;strongly&amp;nbsp;preferred.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;• Ability to translate complex business requirements into platform specifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
